{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>והשבתי</b> — that two tav letters do not combine; one is missing, thus שבתו, for שבת is its root, and likewise וכרתי להם ברית, for כרת is its root. And it is not seen that two tav letters combine to say והשבתתי וכרתתי, for so it ought to have been." "<b>חדשה</b> — it is the head of the month, when the moon is renewed. Also, the tav in it is either defective or assimilated by dagesh in the tav of it."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The Hebrew explicitly marks תוי\"ן (twin tavs) as defective; both והשבתי and וכרתי show elision of the final tav of the root before the conversive-vav suffix.", 1 "The last phrase 'the tav of it' refers to the tav of the following word in the verse; the construction is compressed and the syntax is difficult."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:55.486477793Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}